      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1">The framed manuscript page number [ⲓⲇ] is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke.</p>
        <p n="2">The editors mark ⲉⲧϩⲓⲱϥ as quite uncertain except for ϥ (apparatus).</p>
        <p n="3">The overline of ⲥⲏⲣ (measured) covers ⲥⲏⲣ and not the preceding ⲡ; so also in l. 6.</p>
        <p n="5">Measured overlines: over ⲡⲣⲕⲗⲧⲥ the bar starts after ⲣ (covers ⲕⲗⲧⲥ); over ⲡⲛⲁ it starts after ⲡ (covers ⲛⲁ).</p>
        <p n="7">Measured overline: it covers ⲣⲕⲗⲥ and not the preceding ⲡ; so also in ll. 8 and 18.</p>
        <p n="11">The edition prints an empty pair of brackets (lost, extent not counted) before the four dots; it is kept as a transcriber note.</p>
        <p n="12">The editors suggest, very uncertainly, ⲁⲧⲛ̄ⲡⲁⲛⲧⲓⲇⲓⲕⲟⲥ (apparatus). The last bracket is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="13">Lines 13–14: the editors print, with a brace over both lines, that only slight traces remain; no text is given.</p>
        <p n="14">See l. 13.</p>
        <p n="15">The edition prints empty brackets (lost, extent not counted) at the start, and ends the line with an opening bracket followed by a question mark.</p>
        <p n="16">Empty brackets at the start (lost, extent not counted); the line ends with an opening bracket after ⲛϥ̄.</p>
        <p n="19">The edition prints a closing bracket after the five dots with no opening bracket; the dots are therefore encoded as illegible.</p>
        <p n="21">The editors mark ϯⲛⲟⲩ as uncertain (apparatus). The overline over ⲓ̈ⲏⲥ (measured) starts at ⲓ.</p>
        <p n="22">Empty brackets at the start (lost, extent not counted). The stroke over ⲣ is printed as a peaked stroke.</p>
        <p n="23">Empty brackets at the start (lost, extent not counted).</p>
        <p n="25">ⲝ carries, besides its own wavy top, a separate straight supralinear stroke here (unlike ll. 29 and 31).</p>
        <p n="27">The editors mark ⲧⲟⲩⲁϩⲥ[ⲟ]ⲩ as uncertain (apparatus). After ⲁϥ the edition prints an opening bracket and states that the rest of the line is rubbed off.</p>
        <p n="29">ⲁⲣⲧⲁⲝⲟⲟⲥ (here and l. 31) is restored by the editors after p. 15 l. 28 (apparatus). The strokes over ⲣ at the line ends of ll. 24, 29 and 31 are printed peaked.</p>
        <p n="30">The editors mark ϫⲱⲕ as uncertain (apparatus).</p>
        <p n="32">Measured overline 749–808: it covers ⲣⲕⲗ, not the second ⲡ (37 %) and not ⲥ. The stroke over ϩ in ⲉⲧⲁⲛϩ̀ is printed obliquely.</p>
